## ex8 — a query builder with a grammar

Edit `ex8/solution.ts`. Put the whole sector together: an order that is
enforced, a method that may be called once, and a terminal call that is not
available until the required parts exist.

```ts
export type Part = "from" | "select";

interface Methods<Missing extends Part> {
  readonly __missing?: Missing;
  from(table: string): Builder<Exclude<Missing, "from">>;
  select(columns: readonly string[]): Builder<Exclude<Missing, "select">>;
  where(clause: string): Builder<Missing>;
  build(this: Builder<never>): string;
}

export type Removed<Missing extends Part> =
  | ("from" extends Missing ? "where" : never)
  | ("from" extends Missing ? never : "from")
  | ("select" extends Missing ? never : "select");

export type Builder<Missing extends Part> = Omit<Methods<Missing>, Removed<Missing>>;

export function sql(): Builder<Part>
```

The grammar, in words: `from` comes first and once; `select` once; `where` any
number of times but only after `from`; `build` only when both are supplied.

- `sql().from("orders").select(["id", "total"]).where("total > 0").build()` →
  `"SELECT id, total FROM orders WHERE total > 0"`
- `sql().from("t").select(["*"]).where("a").where("b").build()` → clauses joined
  with `" AND "`
- `sql().where("a")` is a compile error — `where` is not offered before `from`
- `sql().from("t").from("u")` is a compile error
- `sql().from("t").select(["a"]).select(["b"])` is a compile error
- `sql().from("t").build()` is a compile error — `select` is still missing

Include all four negative cases behind `// @ts-expect-error`.

```
